"
I represent the catalog of example models of one line, mirrored from the `cormas/example-catalog` repository on GitHub into the `Catalog` folder of a workspace. Browsing reads only my folder, so it works offline.

## Responsibility:

- I read the line of my version of Cormas: `versions/dev/` for a version in development, `versions/<major>/` for a release.
- I download `catalog.json` and the screenshots it lists, only those that are missing or changed, as told by their hashes, and keep the previous catalog complete and valid when anything fails.
- I choose the version of each model that my Cormas offers: the newest one listed that is made with a Cormas no newer than mine.

## Collaborators:

- `CMWorkspace` gives me its `Catalog` folder with `catalog`, and downloads and updates examples from the versions I offer.
- `CMVersion` gives my line, and compares the versions models are made with.
- `ZnClient` downloads the files over HTTPS, without git.
- `CMWorkspaceError` is what I raise when the catalog cannot be downloaded or is not valid.

## Public API and Key Messages

- `CMCatalog in: aFolder` creates the catalog of this Cormas on a folder; `CMWorkspace>>catalog` is the usual way. `in:for:` takes another version of Cormas.
- `update` mirrors the catalog into my folder.
- `models` returns the models that offer a version to my Cormas, and `offeredVersionOf:` that version, with its url, ref, commit and the Cormas it is made with.
- `isReleasedLine` tells whether the refs are tags of a release or branches in development.

```smalltalk
| catalog |
catalog := CMWorkspace current catalog.
catalog update.
catalog models collect: [ :each | catalog offeredVersionOf: each ]
```

## Internal Representation

- `folder` is the `FileReference` of the `Catalog` folder, holding `catalog.json` and `screenshots/<baseline>.png`.
- `cormasVersion` is the `CMVersion` whose line I read.

### Implementation Points

- `catalog.json` is generated by `tools/catalog.py` in `cormas/example-catalog`. I accept only its format 1; each screenshot path must be `screenshots/<baseline>.png`, with a baseline made of letters and digits.
- Files are written through a temporary file, so that none is ever left half written.
"
Class {
	#name : 'CMCatalog',
	#superclass : 'Object',
	#instVars : [
		'folder',
		'cormasVersion'
	],
	#category : 'Cormas-Workspace',
	#package : 'Cormas-Workspace'
}

{ #category : 'instance creation' }
CMCatalog class >> in: aFolder [
	"Return the catalog of this Cormas, mirrored in aFolder"

	^ self in: aFolder for: CMVersion current
]

{ #category : 'instance creation' }
CMCatalog class >> in: aFolder for: aCormasVersion [
	"Return the catalog read by that version of Cormas, mirrored in aFolder"

	^ self new setFolder: aFolder cormasVersion: aCormasVersion
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> baseUrl [
	"Return where the catalog lines are published. A release could point it elsewhere if the catalog ever moved"

	^ 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cormas/example-catalog/main/versions/'
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> checkScreenshotOf: aModel [

	| baseline |
	baseline := aModel at: 'baseline'.
	((baseline notEmpty and: [
		  baseline allSatisfy: [ :each | each isAlphaNumeric ] ]) and: [
		 (aModel at: 'screenshot') = ('screenshots/' , baseline , '.png') ])
		ifFalse: [
				self error:
					(aModel at: 'screenshot') , ' is not a screenshot of the catalog' ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
CMCatalog >> cormasVersion [

	^ cormasVersion
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> deleteScreenshotsNotIn: models [

	| listed |
	(folder / 'screenshots') exists ifFalse: [ ^ self ].
	listed := models
		          collect: [ :each | (each at: 'baseline') , '.png' ]
		          as: Set.
	(folder / 'screenshots') children do: [ :each |
		(listed includes: each basename) ifFalse: [ each ensureDelete ] ]
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> download: aPath [
	"Return the bytes of a file of the catalog line, from its repository on GitHub"

	^ [
		  ZnClient new
			  beOneShot;
			  beBinary;
			  enforceHttpSuccess: true;
			  get: (self urlOf: aPath) ]
		  on: Error
		  do: [ :error |
				  CMWorkspaceError signal:
					  'Cormas cannot download the catalog (' , error description
					  , ')' ]
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> hashOf: bytes [

	^ (SHA256 hashMessage: bytes) hex
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
CMCatalog >> isReleasedLine [
	"Return whether my line lists tags of a release rather than branches in development"

	^ cormasVersion isDev not
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
CMCatalog >> listsCommit: aCommitId [
	"Return whether the downloaded catalog lists a version at aCommitId made with a Cormas no newer than mine: the Cormas team checked that version with my line"

	^ self models anySatisfy: [ :model |
			  (model at: 'versions') anySatisfy: [ :each |
					  (each at: 'commit') = aCommitId and: [
							  (CMVersion fromString: (each at: 'cormas')) isNoNewerThan:
								  cormasVersion ] ] ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
CMCatalog >> models [
	"Return the models of the downloaded catalog that offer a version to my Cormas, as dictionaries with baseline, summary, screenshot, screenshotHash and versions, or none before the first update"

	| file |
	file := folder / 'catalog.json'.
	file exists ifFalse: [ ^ #(  ) ].
	^ (self modelsIn:
		   (file binaryReadStreamDo: [ :stream | stream upToEnd ])) select: [
		  :each | (self offeredVersionOf: each) notNil ]
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> modelsIn: catalogBytes [
	"Return the models listed in catalog.json, checking its format, and that each screenshot is screenshots/<baseline>.png, so that a catalog never makes Cormas write outside my folder"

	| catalog |
	catalog := [ STONJSON fromString: catalogBytes utf8Decoded ]
		           on: Error
		           do: [ :error |
				           CMWorkspaceError signal:
					           'The catalog is not valid (' , error description , ')' ].
	(catalog isDictionary and: [
		 (catalog at: 'format' ifAbsent: [ nil ]) = 1 ]) ifFalse: [
			CMWorkspaceError signal:
				'The catalog is not valid (format ' , (catalog isDictionary
					 ifTrue: [
					 (catalog at: 'format' ifAbsent: [ 'none' ]) printString ]
					 ifFalse: [ 'none' ]) , ' is not known by this Cormas)' ].
	^ [
		  | models |
		  models := catalog at: 'models'.
		  models do: [ :each | self checkScreenshotOf: each ].
		  models ]
		  on: Error
		  do: [ :error |
				  CMWorkspaceError signal:
					  'The catalog is not valid (' , error description , ')' ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
CMCatalog >> offeredVersionOf: aModel [
	"Return the version of the model that my Cormas offers, as a dictionary with url, ref, commit and cormas: the newest one listed that is made with a Cormas no newer than mine. Return nil when there is none"

	^ (aModel at: 'versions') reversed
		  detect: [ :each |
				  (CMVersion fromString: (each at: 'cormas')) isNoNewerThan:
					  cormasVersion ]
		  ifNone: [ nil ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
CMCatalog >> screenshotOf: aCatalogModel [

	^ folder resolveString: (aCatalogModel at: 'screenshot')
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> setFolder: aFolder cormasVersion: aCormasVersion [

	folder := aFolder.
	cormasVersion := aCormasVersion
]

{ #category : 'updating' }
CMCatalog >> update [
	"Mirror the catalog of example models into my folder: download catalog.json, then each screenshot that is missing or changed, replace catalog.json, and only then delete the screenshots it no longer lists. When anything fails, raise a CMWorkspaceError: the previous catalog stays complete and valid"

	| bytes models |
	bytes := self download: 'catalog.json'.
	models := self modelsIn: bytes.
	CMWorkspaceError whileWritingIn: folder do: [
			models do: [ :each | self updateScreenshotOf: each ].
			self write: bytes to: folder / 'catalog.json'.
			self deleteScreenshotsNotIn: models ]
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> updateScreenshotOf: aModel [
	"Download the screenshot of the model unless my copy has the hash the catalog gives, and check the hash of what was downloaded"

	| file bytes |
	file := folder / 'screenshots' / ((aModel at: 'baseline') , '.png').
	(file exists and: [
			 (self hashOf:
				  (file binaryReadStreamDo: [ :stream | stream upToEnd ]))
			 = (aModel at: 'screenshotHash') ]) ifTrue: [ ^ self ].
	bytes := self download: (aModel at: 'screenshot').
	(self hashOf: bytes) = (aModel at: 'screenshotHash') ifFalse: [
			CMWorkspaceError signal:
				'Cormas cannot download the catalog (' , (aModel at: 'screenshot')
				, ' was not downloaded correctly)' ].
	self write: bytes to: file
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> urlOf: aPath [
	"Return the URL of a file of the catalog line of my version of Cormas"

	^ self baseUrl , cormasVersion line , '/' , aPath
]

{ #category : 'private' }
CMCatalog >> write: bytes to: aFile [
	"Write through a temporary file, so that a file is never left half written"

	| temporary |
	aFile parent ensureCreateDirectory.
	temporary := aFile parent / (aFile basename , '.cormas-tmp').
	temporary ensureDelete.
	temporary binaryWriteStreamDo: [ :stream | stream nextPutAll: bytes ].
	aFile ensureDelete.
	temporary moveTo: aFile
]
